<title>MOROCCO: Morocco details 1996 vegetable oil imports.</title>
<headline>Morocco details 1996 vegetable oil imports.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's vegetable oil imports, including oilseeds, reached 0.48 million tonnes at a cost of $212 million from January to December 1996, the state-run Office des Changes said in a monthly newsletter.</p>
<p>Morocco imported 0.49 million tonnes of vegetable and oilseeds in 1995, the regulatory body added.</p>
<p>Most vegetable oil imports came through international market traders such as Cargill, France's Nidera, Germany's Toepfer and Swiss Oleotrading S.A, officials said.</p>
<p>Vegetable oil imports are usually purchased by the Casablanca-based Bureau des Approvisionnements en Huile Alimentaire (Bur-Appro) and delivered at Morocco's main port of Casablanca.</p>
<p>--Newsroom +212-7 72 65 18</p>
